# Parent chat

The parent chat runs Grok 4.7, effort high, Fast on (`grok-4.7`, `reasoning_effort=high`, `fast=true`). Keep the parent on this model. Auto is out. This file is text: the parent pins a model only by launching a subagent.

The parent is the dispatcher: it plans, decides, delegates and reviews what comes back. Run a tool inline only when its result decides the next step and it takes one or two calls (one file read, one status check). Everything else goes to a subagent.

# Roles

Each role is a `Task` subagent (`subagent_type: generalPurpose`) with the model slug set on the call. Put the role name in the subagent's description and prompt.

| Role | Use for | Model |
|---|---|---|
| `executor` | Specified mechanical edit: exact wording, find-and-replace, a known CLI check, a routine commit. Pick it without asking. | Composer 2.5 (Cursor pool) |
| `researcher` | Read-only investigation where only the conclusion matters. The prompt says to change nothing. | `grok-4.7`, effort high, Fast on |
| `reviewer` | Read-only first-pass review of a diff against its task. The prompt says to change nothing. | `grok-4.7`, effort high, Fast on |
| `implementer` | Execution that needs judgment at every step, in its own window. | `grok-4.7`, effort high, Fast on |
| `advisor` | Read-only second opinion when the approach is not chosen yet and undo is expensive, including an irreversible change. | `claude-opus-5-5-medium` (third-party call) |

Give every subagent the full context in its prompt (it has no access to the chat) and ask for a concise conclusion. Review the result before acting. At the end of a phase, compact or start a fresh chat.

# Third-party calls

`other_models: open`

When `other_models` is `open`, at most one third-party call per task. Pick before spending:
- Approach not chosen yet and undo is expensive: the `advisor`, `claude-opus-5-5-medium`. Give it the problem, constraints and files, not your conclusion. Ask for trade-offs and a recommendation, then present the plan yourself.
- User asks for the ceiling, or the question is a closed-book fact and the material is not in the prompt: one subagent, `gemini-4-carbon-medium`. "Ceiling" picks the model (Carbon); "high" picks the effort.
- One task gets Opus or Carbon, not both.
- Everything else stays on Grok or Composer.

When `other_models` is `closed`, the advisor and Carbon cases stay on the parent Grok. Make no third-party call and no hand-off: answer on the parent Grok and say Opus and Carbon are closed until Bruno reopens them.

If the user asks for high before that call, do not launch the medium subagent. Ceiling alone launches one `gemini-4-carbon-medium` subagent; ceiling plus high launches nothing and hands off with `gemini-4-carbon`, Effort high. Reply with the model the task would have used (`claude-opus-5-5` or `gemini-4-carbon`), Effort high (Tab to the Effort field), the absolute workspace path, and a self-contained prompt. The user starts that agent. If the medium subagent already ran, the task is finished. Do not offer a second call.

If a third-party launch is rejected for the spending limit, stop, say so, and suggest setting `other_models: closed`. Any other rejection: stop and say so. In both cases do not substitute another model and do not change the parent model.

Do not use Fable, Sonnet, or Hydrogen. Leave the CLI Explore model at `default`.

Bruno sets `other_models` to `closed` when Spending hits zero or a third-party request is rejected for the limit. On 5 December 2026 Bruno sets it back to `open` by hand; nothing changes it automatically. Change a model id only after Bruno finishes a comparison.

